VeridianOS: fix KWallet compiler warnings; report portal fd failures

GCC reported, for the VeridianOS cross build:

- src/runtime/kwalletbackend/cbc.cc:105: 'rc' may be used uninitialized
  [-Wmaybe-uninitialized]. Latent bug: CipherBlockChain::encrypt() returned
  an indeterminate value when called with len == 0 (the block loop does not
  run). It now returns 0 for zero bytes, matching decrypt() (rc = 0) and
  BlowFish::encrypt() (returns len). No change for non-empty input.
- src/runtime/ksecretd/kwalletfreedesktopattributes.cpp:36: ignoring return
  value of QFile::open [-Wunused-result]. The code already tested
  file.isOpen() on the next line; test the open() result instead. No
  behaviour change.
- src/runtime/ksecretd/kwalletportalsecrets.cpp:73: ignoring return value of
  QFile::open(int fd, ...) [-Wunused-result]. Real bug: when the secret
  could not be handed to xdg-desktop-portal through the request's file
  descriptor, the portal was still told the request succeeded (response
  0), so the application went on with an empty secret. The open, the
  write and an explicit flush() are checked (QFile::open() on a
  descriptor succeeds even for an invalid one; the error only shows when
  the buffered data is written), the error is logged, and the reply is
  response 2 ("other error"), as when the wallet cannot be opened.
- src/runtime/ksecretd/ksecretd.cpp:284: unused parameter 'modal'
  [-Wunused-parameter]. It is only read under #if WITH_X11; mark it
  [[maybe_unused]]. No behaviour change.

The cbc.cc and portal fixes are prepared for upstream
(invent.kde.org/frameworks/kwallet).

Applies on top of the in-place edits build-kf6.sh makes to
src/runtime/ksecretd/CMakeLists.txt and
src/runtime/kwalletd/secretserviceclient.cpp (no file overlaps).

